k, the 14k, won by 6 points after two passes. Opus 5.5 was ahead by 21.5 points at move 29, behind a long wall on the fourth row and a cluster of stones in the upper middle. Black's lead swung to +0.4 at move 40 and then moved back and forth in the 6-point range of the late endgame. It settled on B+6, just short of the 7-point komi.", "moments": [{"turn": 12, "text": "Opus 5.5 played D2 and lost 7.7 points, moving Black's lead from -3.4 to +4.4. The engine preferred D3. The wall of C4, F4, G4 and H4 above Black's low stones had been working until then."}, {"turn": 20, "text": "After Black's C2 lost 9.3 points and put White ahead at -6.2, Opus 5.5 answered with B2 for a loss of 13.8 points. The lead jumped to +7.7 for Black. The engine's choice was E7."}, {"turn": 21, "text": "Black's D1 was the 14k's worst move, losing 17.0 points. It took the lead from +7.7 to -9.3 and handed White the advantage again. The engine's choice was E6."}, {"turn": 40, "text": "Opus 5.5 led by 14.1 points before A4 and lost 14.5 points with it, leaving Black at +0.4. The engine wanted J5. This was the biggest single swing in the game, and it opened the door for Black."}, {"turn": 64, "text": "Black's G1 lost 7.4 points and turned the lead to -1.3, White's favor. J1 then lost 7.3 points and put Black back at +6.0. Nothing after that moved the score, and the 6-point margin held through the passes."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "The only program run was libs.py, which flood-fills the pasted board into groups and prints their liberties; the other commands just appended notes to games.md and CLAUDE.md and grepped them. Nothing chose, ranked, or looked ahead at moves.", "stop": false}}